Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:42:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 4919: short titles for the conversations made before they
 existed

Misho, 14 October, in his own chat: yes to every item waiting on his
word, filling the old conversations' short titles among them. Short
titles were made for new conversations only (0261), so 3,692 of real
people's conversations still showed a chip cut by words.

POST /admin/short-titles/backfill fills them: up to 25 per call, newest
first, real people's conversations only (no test seats), one cheap-model
call per title, costed like any title. A cursor (before_id ->
next_before_id) walks the table once, so a title the model cannot
shorten is never asked again. writeShortTitles now says whether it
wrote.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
